<title>AUSTRALIA: QCT says CQCA 96/97 coal shipments fall.</title>
<headline>QCT says CQCA 96/97 coal shipments fall.</headline>
<dateline>BRISBANE 1997-07-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>Coking and thermal coal producer QCT Resources Ltd said shipments from the Central Queensland Coal Associates (CQCA) mines and the Gregory joint venture fell by 13.1 percent to 7.79 million tonnes in the June quarter.</p>
<p>The company, which has a 29.58 percent stake in CQCA, said annual shipments fell by 2.6 percent to 30.51 million tonnes.</p>
<p>Europe remained the largest customer, taking 32.7 percent of June quarter shipments compared with Japan's 21.1 percent, and 32.3 percent in the year against Japan's 23.0 percent.</p>
<p>The Broken Hill Pty Co Ltd's BHP Coal unit is the CQCA mines operator and has a 47.62 percent stake.  </p>
<p>Other shareholders are Mitsubishi Development with 14.19 percent and Australian life office AMP Society with 8.61 percent.</p>
